{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfsyl39pz2","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Escalate pipeline has no liveness — guidance never auto stales when origin task done or note superseded","summary":"Review of the request_guidance / guidance escalation pipeline found two structural gaps matching the user's complaint (\"escalates many things, does not recognize it is being worked on\"). MODE 1 over-escalation: the ask-gate predict corpus is ONLY category:preference notes (lib/ask-gate-recall.js runAskGate), so a situational/technical blocker with no matching preference note falls to no-preference -> ASK; and a worker self-asserting a trigger like scopeExpansion forces a hard-override (lib/ask-gate.js hardOverride) that bypasses prediction entirely. The FB-3 blocker answer existed in the graph as a correction note (note-mqfh9nmj87j) the gate never consults. MODE 2 no liveness: addGuidance (lib/overlay.js) stamps NO origin task or triggering-note key, so the daemon cannot tell which task a question is about; there is NO sweepStaleGuidance among the per-tick sweeps (daemon.js sweepStaleClaims/Verdicts/FailedTasks/Loops), so a blocking text-guidance is never auto-resolved when its origin task goes done/merged or its note is superseded; and plain text escalations do not dedup (only dup-cluster by signature and follow-up by task_key do). Concrete instance: guidance g-mqfh5q85-x7gk sat pending after its blocker note was superseded and the deliverable shipped (task /7) — resolved only by manual consolidation. FIX (user approved full scope): A stamp origin_task+origin_notes at the seam; B sweepStaleGuidance auto-resolve on done/merged origin or superseded note (mirror sweepStaleVerdicts); C dedup plain escalations by origin_task+question hash; D widen predict corpus to decision/correction notes so already-answered blockers auto-resolve.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T22:46:26.373Z","vec":[-0.1467113196849823,-0.02471022866666317,-0.00658015534281730